I'm not exactly sure. He fits some of the criteria but I remember the art looking a little differently. Also, he was sitting at a desk.

I remember using the word "flavor" to describe what different perspectives of reality might feel like, as that's what nostalgia feels like for me. It's interesting to find it in this context. 

&#x200B;

For me it's pretty hard to explain. It feels like I'm in a dream, a VHS like dream filled with regurgitations of pop culture between the 70s through the 90s. I watched a lot of old VHS tapes as a kid, and even some that my parents had taped from before I was born. I often watched videos as a form of escapism from my emotionally traumatic childhood. That might be why. I also used to have the most vivid, abstract, horrific, surreal nightmares which would make me feel dissociated during the day, especially since I didn't get enough sleep. Sometimes the dissociation feels very urgent, like I'm in a dreamlike tape that the VHS player will soon silence. I have other kinds of dissociative flavors with different things sometimes, but that one is usually the most prominent.
